**Proposition 8.3 (complete same-run accounting).** PVC.9–11 and
Definition 8.1 evaluate one full native opcode/purpose/fee/storage vector
at every original or added cut. In particular they count all old source
preparation, retained dead banks, interpreter/serializer work, selectors,
registry material, simultaneous sender/mailbox/receiver and all returns.

Proof. Each actual native row has one purpose and one receipt. The
compiler expansion gives its complete successor before the next schema
is evaluated. Addition in sequence therefore partitions, rather than
double-counts, occurrences. EX and finite-bit constructors have their
actual net additions. All new helpers reduce to finite instruction
expansions and their tests/metadata; no graph or historical row is charged
as one word instruction. Induction on actual rows gives PVC.9, and the
disjoint channel body count gives PVC.11. The source clone's RD/MR rows
are additional to the one actual external ingress, without inventing a
second IN. Historical virtual receipts are word data; their production
has its own real rows/receipts already in this same count. ∎

